  "described": {
    "alt_text": "A grey marker drawing in a spiral sketchbook of a camouflage patterned cactus body with striped, twisted arms ending in spines.",
    "description": "A square photograph of a spiral bound sketchbook page on a wooden table. A rounded cactus body rises from the bottom of the page, patterned with a camouflage of grey, lilac and white blobs outlined in black. From it grow five or six twisted arms with diagonal stripes, like candy canes or barber poles, each ending in a cluster of spines. A squared lobe sits at lower right. Grey marker shading, black outlines, bare paper background.",
    "impression": "A cactus in camouflage with striped tentacles, somewhere between a plant, a sea anemone and a sock puppet. The stripes make the arms look like they are rotating. The oddest of the marker studies, in a good way.",
